  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>Parasitemia determined from conventional light microscopy: Clinical correlation</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 99.9971%; height: 200.833px;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 33.2869%;\"><col style=\"width: 33.2869%;\"><col style=\"width: 33.2869%;\"></colgroup>\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.4722px;\">\n<td>Parasitemia&nbsp;</td>\n<td>Parasites/ul</td>\n<td>Clinical Correlation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.4722px;\">\n<td>0.0001 - 0.0004%&nbsp;</td>\n<td>5 - 20&nbsp;</td>\n<td>One set (TBF+THBF) of negative blood films does not rule out a<br>malaria infection.<br>Test should be repeated</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.4722px;\">\n<td>0.002%&nbsp;</td>\n<td>100</td>\n<td>Patients may be symptomatic below this level</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.4722px;\">\n<td>0.2%&nbsp;</td>\n<td>10,000</td>\n<td>Level above which immune patients will exhibit symptoms</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.4722px;\">\n<td>2%&nbsp;</td>\n<td>1,00,000</td>\n<td>Maximum parasitemia of P.vivax and P.ovale (infect young RBCs<br>only )</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.4722px;\">\n<td>2 - 5%&nbsp;</td>\n<td>1,00,000 - 2,50,000</td>\n<td>Hyperparasitemia, severe malaria, increased mortality</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>10%&nbsp;</td>\n<td>5,00,000&nbsp;</td>\n<td>Exchange transfusion may be considered, high mortality.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
